guide.lapis_drake=§dLapis Drake
guide.lapis_drake_general=The Lapis Drake is part of the crystal drake family that lives deep underground. Its reclusive nature makes it aggressive toward humans and impossible to tame. Slaying one rewards you with a fragment of its power. Like its kin, it stands guard over a powerful altar buried in the depths (see Special Materials for more details).
guide.emerald_drake=§5Emerald Drake
guide.emerald_drake_general=The Emerald Drake is part of the crystal drake family that dwells deep within lush underground caverns. Revered for its wisdom and rarity, it fiercely guards the riches of the earth (see Special Materials for more details). Though untameable, defeating one may yield a fragment of its power.
guide.gold_drake=§4Gold Drake
guide.gold_drake_general=The Gold Drake is part of the crystal drake found both in the blazing caverns of the Nether and the deepest Overworld mines. Its radiant scales glimmer with greed and power, and its territory is guarded with relentless fury. While it cannot be tamed, those who defeat it may uncover a fragment of its power and the ancient altar all crystal drakes protect (see Special Materials).
guide.quartz_drake=§2Quartz Drake
guide.quartz_drake_general=The Quartz Drake is part of the crystal drake that thrives in the fiery depths of the Nether. Its crystalline body radiates intense heat, and it attacks any intruder without hesitation. Though untameable, defeating it yields a fragment of its power. It too guards the ancient altar shared among the crsytal drakes (see Special Materials).
guide.redstone_drake=§bRedstone Drake
guide.redstone_drake_general=The Redstone Drake is part of the crystal drake infused with the earth’s living energy. Its body crackles with power, glowing faintly in the dark tunnels it calls home. These dragons are highly aggressive and cannot be tamed. Like all crystal drakes, it protects the ancient altar pulsing with energy beneath the world (see Special Materials).

guide.general_egg1=Dragons eggs can be found arround the world in side dragon nests.\n\nThe hatching process is started by interacting with the egg.\n\n
guide.general_egg2=Starting the hatching process will unlock everything there is to know about this egg type. In case it doesn't you can simply interact with the hatching egg while holing the guidebook to unlock it.\n\n
guide.general_egg3=After around 20 minutes, when the egg hatches, it will unlock everything there is to know about the dragon type.\n\n
guide.general_egg4=If interacted with while sneaking then the egg turn into its item form so it can be picked up again.\n\n\n
guide.general_egg5=Eggs can change their type upon starting the hatching process but only under the right conditions.
